 (including Ollama), Gemini support, and adapters for OpenAI and Anthropic
- Structured sales-order extraction, deterministic normalization, field evidence, confidence, and validation
- Human review queue, split-pane document review, line-item editing, approval, rejection, and reprocessing
- Hard validation approval gates with reasoned, role-restricted, immutable supervisor overrides
- Catalog/reference-data foundations and outbound integration profiles
- Operational dashboards, processing analytics, audit events, health probes, quotas, and provider status
- SQLite/local-filesystem development mode and PostgreSQL/S3-compatible production mode
- Docker Compose, CI, tests, deployment notes, security controls, and release gates

## Fastest local start

```bash
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up --build
```

Open `http://localhost:5173` and sign in with:

- Email: `admin@demo.example`
- Password: `demo1234`

The default configuration uses deterministic heuristic extraction, so the app works without any cloud key. To use Ollama:

```bash
docker compose --profile local-ai up --build
# In another terminal, pull a model:
docker exec -it soa-build-ollama-1 ollama pull qwen2.5:7b-instruct
```

Set `DEFAULT_LLM_PROVIDER=local` in `.env`. For Gemini, set `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `DEFAULT_LLM_PROVIDER=gemini`.

## Development without Docker

```bash
cp .env.example .env
make install
make dev
```

The API runs on port 8000, the web app on port 5173, and a dedicated worker processes queued documents.

Run the complete validation suite before publishing a change:

```bash
make check
make smoke # requires the local API and worker to be running
```

## Architecture

The repository uses a modular-monolith control plane and a separate worker process:

```text
Browser → React web app → FastAPI API → PostgreSQL/SQLite
                              │
                              ├─ object storage (local or S3/R2)
                              └─ durable database job queue → worker
                                                           ├─ native PDF parser
                                                           ├─ Tesseract OCR
                                                           ├─ local/Gemini/OpenAI/Claude extraction
                                                           ├─ validation and confidence
                                                           └─ review or auto-approval
```

All provider and infrastructure choices sit behind adapters. Moving from free-tier services to paid capacity is configuration and migration work—not an application rewrite.

